third_party/libsync: do not redefine ETIME.

Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), not submitted upstream.
Source: Chromium electron-source tree under EmberBSD.
EmberBSD sys/errno.h already defines ETIME, so the Linux-oriented fallback
in sync.c trips -Werror,-Wmacro-redefined. Only define it when missing.
The BSD port also stubs out the ioctl paths, leaving static helpers unused
(-Werror,-Wunused-function); silence that warning for this file.

--- a/third_party/libsync/src/sync.c	2026-10-28 02:57:09.361812998 +0300
+++ b/third_party/libsync/src/sync.c	2026-10-28 02:59:37.087216123 +0300
@@ -36,7 +36,11 @@
 
 #define __u32 uint32_t
 #define	__s32 int32_t
+/* EmberBSD: the BSD port stubs out the ioctl paths, leaving helpers unused. */
+#pragma clang diagnostic ignored "-Wunused-function"
+#ifndef ETIME /* EmberBSD: sys/errno.h already defines ETIME */
 #define ETIME ETIMEDOUT
+#endif
 
